    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20731" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hippocrătes</span></b> , is,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἱπποκράτης</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the celebrated Greek
				physician of Cos</i>, <i>founder of the art of
				medicine</i>, Cels. praef.; <i><span class="en">Cic. de
				Or. 3, 33, 132</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 3, 6,
			64</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hippocrătĭcus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Hippocrates</i>, <i>Hippocratic</i>: laniena, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 10, 497.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A Syracusan</i>, <i>brother of
				Epicydes</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 24, 35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">36 al.</span></i></div>
